HST Office: the Print page of the File panel shows the state of each printer: a dot before every printer name of
its printer list and a short text beside the selected printer ("Trạng thái:").

- Dots: 10 px across at 100 % (with the DPI scale and the list's font size), centred on the text line, with a 1 px
  darker outline so amber and grey show on light, dark and highlighted rows.
- Green: ready. Amber: busy or paused (printing, processing, warming up, toner low...). Red: offline or an error
  that stops it (paper jam, out of paper, door open, out of toner, offline, stopped CUPS queue). Grey: unknown.
- Text: Sẵn sàng / Đang bận / Tạm dừng / Ngoại tuyến / Lỗi: hết giấy, kẹt giấy, nắp máy in đang mở, hết mực / Sắp
  hết mực / Không rõ trạng thái (en: Ready, Busy, Paused, Offline, Error: ..., Toner low, Status unknown), shown
  before the label's own text ("Sẵn sàng — Máy in mặc định") and as the tooltip and accessible description of the
  printer list, so colour is never the only sign.
- Data (vcl hstprinterstatusquery.cxx), on a thread of its own when the page opens and each time the list drops
  down; dots are grey until the answer arrives, nothing waits on the main thread:
  - Windows: the spooler's PRINTER_INFO_2 Status bits and the PRINTER_ATTRIBUTE_WORK_OFFLINE attribute
    (26.8.3.1's queue list enumerates level 4 without a state; its GetPrinterQueueState asks synchronously);
  - Linux/BSD: CUPS printer-state (idle/processing/stopped), printer-is-accepting-jobs and printer-state-reasons
    (26.8.3.1's unx queue info leaves the state empty); the profile's generic printer is no CUPS queue: grey;
  - macOS and others: grey (the queue info has no state there).
- Test runs only: HST_TEST_PRINTER_STATES="<printer>=ready|busy|paused|offline|paperout|unknown;..." overrides
  the system for those printers (screenshots on a host without a print server).
- Mapping flags to state and text: vcl::hst::ClassifyPrinterStatus / PrinterStatusText (hstprinterstatus.cxx).
- vcl hstprintpanel.ui: the printer list is a GtkComboBox over a list store with an image column (text, id,
  pixbuf, surface; the dot before the name), so GTK shows the dots too (a GtkComboBoxText has no image column).
- Hook: PrintDialog (panel form only) owns a vcl::hst::PrinterStatusView over its printer list and status label;
  updatePrinterText tells it the selection changed.

License: include/vcl/hstprinterstatus.hxx, vcl/inc/hstprinterstatus.hrc, vcl/source/window/hstprinterstatus.cxx and
vcl/source/gdi/hstprinterstatusquery.cxx are HST Office code (LicenseRef-HST-Proprietary); the modified files keep
their license (MPL-2.0).
Test: CppunitTest_vcl_hst_print_panel testPrinterStatusMapping, testPrinterStatusInPanel;
tests/unit/test_print_printer_status.py.
